index 7dd10a9..05ffa6f 100644
--- a/docs/test-suite-performance.md
+++ b/docs/test-suite-performance.md
@@ -100,12 +100,108 @@ The profiling helper used here lives in `docs/profiling/event_prof.rb`
 
 ## Ideas for future phases (not done yet)
 
-- Factories (phase 2): `:status` fabricator creates a `:bookmark` per status;
+- Factories (next phase): `:status` fabricator creates a `:bookmark` per status;
   `:user` fabricator creates 2 `:login_activity` records per user — likely
   intentional vs upstream; trimming these is a factories-phase item.
 - `Rails.cache.clear` + `redis.del(redis.keys)` after every example (~1-2 s
   total): could be made conditional on redis/cache actually being touched.
-- `spec/requests` phase: same sidekiq-mode treatment (many request specs may
-  rely on inline — audit and tag).
 - Consider `test-prof` (`before_all`) for heavy shared setups
   (e.g. `spec/models/trends/*`) if it can be added to the bundle.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 2 — spec/requests (2025 run)
+
+### Baseline (before any optimization work), `bundle exec rspec spec/requests`
+
+Measured with phase-1 optimizations disabled (`RUBY_YJIT_ENABLE=0
+RAILS_LOG_LEVEL=debug`, Sidekiq `:inline` — the historical defaults for
+request specs):
+
+- **3 min 9 s** — 1877 examples, 0 failures (files took ~2.9 s to load)
+- With only phase-1 optimizations active (YJIT + `log_level :info`, Sidekiq
+  still `:inline`): **2 min 17.1 s** — i.e. phase 1 alone gave requests ~27%.
+
+### Profiling findings (spec/requests)
+
+Instrumented with the updated `docs/profiling/event_prof.rb` (see note below)
+at the phase-1 state (inline Sidekiq), total example+hook time 131.6 s:
+
+| Event             | Time    | Count   | Notes |
+|-------------------|---------|---------|-------|
+| Fabrication       | 98.9 s  | 11,030 creates + 7,548 builds | includes inline jobs fired by model callbacks (nested) |
+| **Sidekiq inline**| **43.2 s** | **7,753 jobs** | ~1/3 of example time! Distribution/notification/mail/webhook workers |
+| SQL (non-schema)  | 28.0 s  | 204,873 | |
+| request_process   | 26.6 s  | 1,956   | full rack stack per HTTP request; inherent |
+| ActiveJob inline  | 6.3 s   | 150     | mailers via the sidekiq AJ adapter |
+| Redis total       | 0.8 s   | 12,306  | negligible |
+
+NOTE (tooling): Sidekiq 8 moved the inline path from
+`Sidekiq::Client#raw_push_inline` to `TestingClient#atomic_push`, so the
+phase-1 event_prof no longer recorded inline time. The profiler now wraps
+`atomic_push` (counting only when `Sidekiq::Testing.inline?`),
+`ActiveJob::Base#perform_now` and
+`ActionDispatch::Integration::Session#process`. Use `def x(...)`/`super`
+forwarding — `def x(*)` silently breaks kwargs (e.g. rack-test `process`).
+
+### Optimization applied (config-level + tags only)
+
+**`spec/rails_helper.rb`** — request specs now default to
+`Sidekiq::Testing.fake!`, same as model specs; `sidekiq: :inline` metadata
+opts back in. Other spec types keep the historical `:inline` default.
+
+Safety notes:
+- rspec-sidekiq clears fake queues before every example
+  (`clear_all_enqueued_jobs` defaults to true) — no cross-example leakage.
+- Specs asserting enqueues via `have_enqueued_sidekiq_job` /
+  `enqueue_sidekiq_job` already call `Sidekiq.testing!(:fake)` inside the
+  example — unaffected by the default change.
+- Flipping the default surfaced 41 failing examples; all were genuinely
+  relying on inline execution and are now tagged `sidekiq: :inline`:
+  - `spec/requests/api/v1/notifications_spec.rb` (top-level describe) and
+    `spec/requests/api/v2/notifications_spec.rb` (top-level describe) —
+    notifications are created by `LocalNotificationWorker` after
+    Favourite/Reblog/Follow/PostStatus service calls in `before` hooks.
+  - `spec/requests/api/v2/notifications/accounts_spec.rb` — same reason.
+  - `spec/requests/api/v1/conversations_spec.rb` (`GET /api/v1/conversations`)
+    — conversation rows materialize via workers.
+  - `spec/requests/api/v1/timelines/home_spec.rb` (`context 'when the
+    timeline is available'`) — home feed entries are pushed by
+    `FeedInsertWorker`.
+  - `spec/requests/api/v1/statuses/favourites_spec.rb` (2 unfavourite
+    examples) — `Api::V1::Statuses::FavouritesController#destroy` delegates
+    the destroy to `UnfavouriteWorker`.
+  - `spec/requests/api/v1/admin/account_actions_spec.rb` (5 contexts) and
+    `spec/requests/api/v1/reports_spec.rb` (`'creates a report'`) —
+    `capture_emails` requires the mailer job to really run (same rule as
+    phase 1).
+- Gotcha: metadata on a `shared_examples` definition is **not** inherited
+  through `it_behaves_like` (rspec-core 3.13) — tag the enclosing
+  example group instead.
+- `spec/requests/admin/confirmations_spec.rb` uses `capture_emails` but only
+  asserts the list is empty — passes under `:fake`, no tag needed.
+
+### Results, full `spec/requests` (1877 examples)
+
+| Run | Total time | vs baseline |
+|-----|-----------|-------------|
+| Baseline (pre-optimization) | 3 min 9 s | — |
+| Phase-1 only (YJIT + log level) | 2 min 17.1 s | -27% |
+| + fake Sidekiq default (seeded) | 1 min 48.8 s / 1 min 47.8 s | **-42%** |
+
+Post-change profile: sidekiq_inline 43.2 s → 16.9 s (7,753 → 1,181 jobs,
+remainder lives in the tagged specs), fabricate 98.9 s → 73.2 s, SQL
+204,873 → 136,102 queries. Example+hook time 131.6 s → 105.3 s.
+
+Slowest remaining groups are flat (~0.2-0.3 s/example; signature
+verification RSA signing, ActivityPub replies, tagged notification specs) —
+no new shared bottleneck. Fabrication dominates; that is the factories
+phase.
+
+### Combined models + requests
+
+| | Baseline | Now | Speed-up |
+|---|---------|-----|----------|
+| spec/models | 2 min 44.7 s | ~50 s (re-verified 50.1 s, 0 failures) | 3.3x |
+| spec/requests | 3 min 9 s | ~1 min 48 s | 1.75x |
+| **Total** | **5 min 53.7 s** | **~2 min 38 s** | **2.24x** |
